From: OHOS Dev <dev@ohos.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0118] Fix test_compileall HardlinkDedupTestsBase missing hardlink guard

HardlinkDedupTestsBase.test_hardlink() lacks @skipUnless(_can_hardlink)
that other methods in the same class already have. On HMDFS where
hardlink(2) returns EPERM, _can_hardlink=False, but this test still runs
and fails with AssertionError: is_hardlink() != True.

Fix: Insert @skipUnless(_can_hardlink) before test_hardlink() in
HardlinkDedupTestsBase class (matching the pattern used by sibling methods).

---
 Lib/test/test_compileall.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Lib/test/test_compileall.py b/Lib/test/test_compileall.py
index abcdef..1234567 100644
--- a/Lib/test/test_compileall.py
+++ b/Lib/test/test_compileall.py
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ class HardlinkDedupTestsBase:
         self.assertEqual(is_hardlink(pycs[1], pycs[2]),
                          not docstring)
 
+    @skipUnless(_can_hardlink, 'Filesystem does not support hardlinks')
     def test_hardlink(self):
         # Test deduplication on all combinations
         for code, docstring, assertion in self.iter_codes():

--
